<section id="safety" class="city-section" aria-labelledby="safety-title">
  <h2 id="safety-title">What keeps workers in line</h2>
  <ol class="safety-list">
    <li>
      <strong>Worktrees:</strong> every worker edits its own git worktree and branch; nothing reaches your branch until the orchestrator re-runs the tests and merges.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Shell allowlist:</strong> opencode workers may only run test and build runners and read-only commands; everything else is denied. agy workers get no shell at all.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Edits stay inside the worktree:</strong> opencode file tools outside it are denied (shell runners are not covered, so this is a guard, not a sandbox).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Circuit breaker:</strong> an opencode worker that keeps hitting denied commands or failing tool calls is stopped and handed back to the orchestrator.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No secrets to cold workers:</strong> auth, secrets and data work stays on Claude subagents, and the orchestrator is told never to copy <code>.env</code> files into a worktree.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Guards, not a sandbox:</strong> in Claude Code the guard hooks block obvious writes and fetch-and-run commands; a test runner can still run any code in your project.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="safety-source">Where to check: <code>scripts/agy-task</code> and <code>claude/hooks/guard.py</code> for the guards, <code>core/agents/lead-dev-hybrid.md</code> and <code>core/skills/hybrid-delegate</code> for the routing rules.</p>
</section>

